      "source": [
        "## 1. My lane as an ML task (type)\n",
        "\n",
        "*Classification, clustering, ranking, or scoring — which one, and why?*"
      ],
      "id": "d6QNwwHWWd-t"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Ranking / scoring\n",
        "\n",
        "The goal is to prioritize content pages for editorial review so that editors can focus on pages that may need attention most. The model would assign each page a priority score and rank pages accordingly. The output supports editorial decision making; it does not automatically prove that a page will decline."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ehOBIzQdcZAB"
      },
      "id": "ehOBIzQdcZAB"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "3IFrWL19Wd-z"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 2. Target or proxy\n",
        "\n",
        "*What would you predict? Where does that label come from — observed outcome or a defined rule?*"
      ],
      "id": "3IFrWL19Wd-z"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The ideal target is an observed future outcome, such as whether a content page experiences a meaningful decline in performance during a later time window. The target should be measured independently of the features used to rank pages. The starter dataset contains trailing 90 day metrics, so I must verify whether a valid future outcome exists before claiming predictive performance. If it does not, I will treat the ranking as exploratory decision-support rather than a validated prediction."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "s6_UUcCecIkB"
      },
      "id": "s6_UUcCecIkB"
    },
