      },
      "source": [
        "## 3. Success metric\n",
        "\n",
        "*One metric you can defend. What number means 'good'?*"
      ],
      "id": "JAgkGiGiWd-0"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "precision@K.\n",
        "\n",
        "Precision@K measures the proportion of the top K ranked pages that meet the independently observed outcome of interest. For example, Precision@10 measures how many of the ten highest priority pages actually experience the specified future outcome. I will compare the result with a baseline and report the measured value only after the target and evaluation period are validated. If no independent outcome label exists, Precision@K cannot yet be claimed as a valid success metric."
